{"term":"suppress","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:18ce4fd59bd55582f6","definition":"To put an end to, especially with force, to crush, do away with; to prohibit, subdue.","example":"Political dissent was brutally suppressed.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["abolish","clamp down","eliminate","bury","quash","squash"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosuppress","desuppress","immunosuppress","myelosuppress","resuppress","suppressable","suppressant","suppressible","suppression","suppressive","suppressogenic","suppressor","suppressory","unsuppress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suppress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:7edd2598cf2250364e","definition":"To restrain or repress, such as laughter or an expression.","example":"I struggled to suppress my smile.","pos":"verb","synonyms":["curtail","stifle","behedge","guard","govern","smother","bind","chasten","choke back","check","inhibit","catch","contain","vanquish","cork","curb","quench","quell","bury","curtail","dampen","hamshackle","hold back","hold down","limit","repress","restrain","restrict","shackle","stay","stifle","stop","straiten","subdue","suppress","throttle","underbring","withhold","withstrain"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["cosuppress","desuppress","immunosuppress","myelosuppress","resuppress","suppressable","suppressant","suppressible","suppression","suppressive","suppressogenic","suppressor","suppressory","unsuppress"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/suppress#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:b433abf80c0815c903","definition":"To exclude undesirable thoughts from one's mind.","example":"He unconsciously suppressed his memories of abuse.","pos":"verb","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"